      "description": "In Tongxiao Township, Hutoushan Park features a Shinto shrine left from the Japanese colonial period. The shrine is built along the hills of Hutoushan, and its main hall, offering hall, worship hall, administrative office, approach path, and torii gate have primarily retained their original appearance, making it one of the few shrines preserved after the war.\nAfter Taiwan's retrocession, the government, to diminish the cultural influence left by the colonizers, converted the worship hall of the Tongxiao Shrine into the Tongxiao Township Martyrs' Shrine, dedicated to the revered Koxinga (Zheng Chenggong). As a result, locals often refer to it as the \"Zheng Chenggong Temple.\" The \"worship hall\" exterior was transformed into a traditional Minnan-style building, featuring red brick walls and a roof with swallowtail ridges. The roof ridges are adorned with the national emblem, the \"Blue Sky with a White Sun.\" The Japanese-style stone lanterns along both sides of the approach path, together with the torii gate stone pillars and the surrounding greenery, evoke a sense of tranquility and harmony. This further enhances the shrine's antique charm, immersing visitors in a Japanese cultural atmosphere.",
